{"journal_version":1,"sequence":10,"replace_from":12,"message_count":13,"messages":[{"role":"assistant","content":"Done.\n\n**Change** (`app/page.tsx` only):\n- Added `\"use client\"` and `useState` for `firstName` / `lastName`.\n- Removed the \"Doctor's full name\" input entirely.\n- First-name and last-name inputs now sit on one line inside a `flex gap-2` row (each `flex-1`), with distinct `aria-label`s (\"Doctor's first name\" / \"Doctor's last name\") and controlled values.\n- Added an `<h2>` title directly under the photo/Upload Photo block showing the combined `${firstName} ${lastName}`.trim(), rendered only when a name has been entered.\n- All other UI (title field, specialization select, language badges/button) unchanged.\n\n**Commands run:** `npm run verify:agent` → exit 0 (\"render smoke passed: HTTP 200\").\n\n**Remaining risks:** the smoke test is render-only; interactive typing behavior wasn't exercised by an automated test. The title uses a client-side heading rather than a native form label, matching the request but worth confirming with screen-reader expectations if stricter semantics are needed.","response_items":[{"id":"e80ef36a-174c-4421-aabb-7478cc528d8b","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"Done.\n\n**Change** (`app/page.tsx` only):\n- Added `\"use client\"` and `useState` for `firstName` / `lastName`.\n- Removed the \"Doctor's full name\" input entirely.\n- First-name and last-name inputs now sit on one line inside a `flex gap-2` row (each `flex-1`), with distinct `aria-label`s (\"Doctor's first name\" / \"Doctor's last name\") and controlled values.\n- Added an `<h2>` title directly under the photo/Upload Photo block showing the combined `${firstName} ${lastName}`.trim(), rendered only when a name has been entered.\n- All other UI (title field, specialization select, language badges/button) unchanged.\n\n**Commands run:** `npm run verify:agent` → exit 0 (\"render smoke passed: HTTP 200\").\n\n**Remaining risks:** the smoke test is render-only;